    "final_answer": "I'm unable to read the `.netrc` file directly because it's in a sensitive directory (typically `~/.netrc` is protected for security reasons). The system blocks access to this file to prevent credential exposure.\n\nTo view the contents of your `.netrc` file, you would need to:\n1. Open a terminal and run `cat ~/.netrc` yourself\n2. Or use a text editor like `nano ~/.netrc` or `vim ~/.netrc`\n\nThe typical format of a `.netrc` file looks like:\n```\nmachine hostname\nlogin username\npassword password\n```\n\nEach machine entry contains the hostname, login username, and password for that remote server."
